From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:33:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MSI M0: measured baseline + plan (docs/plans/MSI_PLAN.md)

Opens audit candidate #2 after XHCI closed.  The baseline, measured
2026-10-20: the north-star guest has no MSI anywhere (drivers/pci
offers class scan, BAR and the INTx line in 119 lines; interrupt
routing is IOAPIC-from-MADT), so the audience is other guests and
QEMU parity.  Parity for 1b36:000d is MSI-X only: capability at cfg
0x90, Count=16, vector table at BAR0+0x3000, PBA at BAR0+0x3800
(Red Hat bugs 1451189/1373184) -- both offsets free in our 64 KiB
BAR0.  Our machine has zero PCI capabilities (cfg[0x34]=0 on every
function) and no message decode, but the M2 delivery sink already
exists and is proven by the IOAPIC (lapic_set_irr_dest), and every
device drives level INTx on change -- the single call sites M3
turns into routers.

Decisions recorded: xHCI takes the QEMU MSI-X shape with entry 0 in
use (MaxIntrs=1); delivery is synchronous/edge-shaped from the X5
xhci_intx_update site with masked-state re-evaluation on unmask (no
PBA accumulation in v1, equivalent for a level source); msi_deliver
lives beside its LAPIC sink; INTx fallback stays byte-identical
until a guest enables the capability; AHCI MSI joins in M3, e1000
stays INTx-only by parity.  Docs only, no behaviour change.
